        <DemoExample Title="Draggable" RazorCode="@example11RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example11CsharpCode" Id="example11">
            <div>
                <b>Draggable</b> lets the user move the Modal around, for the surfaces that have to be pushed aside
                to see what they are covering - a picker held open next to the field it fills in, a tool window.
                The whole Modal is the handle by default, which takes the text selection and the scrolling inside
                it with the drag; <b>DragElementSelector</b> names a part of the content to drag it by instead,
                and leaves the rest of it usable.
            </div>
            <br />
